"""nomada: move papers between Zotero and a SuperNote Nomad through a synced folder.

    new paper in Zotero  --push-->  SuperNote/INBOX   --> read + annotate on Nomad
                                                                  | export
    Zotero item (original + annotated)  <--pull--  SuperNote/EXPORT <-+

`push` copies the PDF of every Zotero item tagged `tag_new` into INBOX, records
filename -> item key, and moves the item's tag to `tag_inreview`. `pull`
attaches each PDF found in EXPORT to the item recorded under the same filename,
moves the tag to `tag_reviewed`, archives the INBOX original into
INBOX/_archived, and moves the export into EXPORT/_processed. `note` writes a
Markdown literature note for each item tagged `tag_reviewed`, with the
highlighted text and an image of each group of handwritten marks; `pull` does
the same for each paper it imports when `note_on_pull` is set.

Reading uses Zotero's local API. Tagging, and attaching with the "localwrite"
backend, use the Local Write API add-on
(github.com/dzackgarza/zotero-local-write-api). The "webapi" backend attaches
through the Zotero Web API instead.
"""
